gpui_windows: Fence UTF-16 text input to its target

A surrogate pair split across WM_CHAR messages combined with a high
surrogate typed into a different field, window or text context. Pairs now
combine only within one text target, identified by focus and the new
`InputHandler::text_input_context_generation`; focus loss, deactivation,
a disabled IME and a layout change drop a pending half. Ending an IME
composition removes only the remaining marked text, not a committed
selection, and keys the IME processes (VK_PROCESSKEY) are not dispatched
as key events.

The input_lifecycle example drives these messages against a real window.

Newport needs it for Remote apps on Windows: text input forwards into
Linux text fields that change without GPUI focus moving.

text_input_context_generation has a default of 0, which keeps focus as
the only fence; other platforms do not call it.

Remove when upstream gpui_windows fences surrogate pairs to their target.

